confirmation meets the success criteria.\n\n**Wait, one constraint:** \"Specific model, material or scene results must not be extrapolated to other objects or settings without basis.\" I must be careful not to say cOFM works in humans for ICI just because it worked in glioblastoma xenografts. I must state it as a methodological example.\n\n**Another constraint:** \"For 'whether there is already a certain type of study/result' questions, finding one eligible instance can answer; several papers not mentioning, or an earlier review saying none at that time, cannot answer whether it exists now.\"\n*   P0592 (2025) and P0610 (2025) are very recent. They explicitly state the gap exists *now* (\"are nascent\", \"lacking\"). This is strong evidence for the current state.\n*   P0610 mentions a TMAO study. This is an \"eligible instance\" for *microbial metabolites in TME*, though not inosine/SCFA.\n*   So I can answer: \"For inosine/SCFAs, it is a gap. For TMAO, there is an example.\"\n\n**Structure:**\n1.  `quantitative_comparisons`: List the numbers found (L-arginine, cOFM metabolite counts).\n2.  `usable_content`: Synthesize the findings.\n3.  `decision`: `direct_use`.\n4.  `reason`: Materials confirm the gap and provide the TMAO exception.\n\n**Check `quantitative_comparisons` requirement:** \"groups is [{group:原文组名或缩写,value:紧邻该组的结果含单位}]\".\n*   P0592: \"low serum L-arginine concentration (less than 42 μM)\". Group: \"low serum L-arginine\", Value: \"< 42 μM\".\n*   P0600: \"over 30 % of the metabolome found to be altered in tumors compared to controls\". Group: \"tumors\", Value: \"> 30% altered\". \"281 were found in brain ISF\". Group: \"brain ISF\", Value: \"281 metabolites\".\n*   P0610: No specific numbers in the provided text snippets for TMAO.\n\n**Check `usable_content` requirement:** \"First present findings or arguments that can distinguish different studies... Do not synthesize results of multiple different objects... into a universal mechanism.\"\n*   Distin